# Deployment standards

When adding or changing deployment docs, scripts that start/restart services, or process management:

## Principles (industry standards)

- **Twelve-Factor (Processes):** Production runs under container orchestration (Docker Compose). See [12factor.net/processes](https://12factor.net/processes).
- **Single owner per service/port:** Only Docker Compose manages service lifecycles and port allocation. Scripts must delegate to Docker Compose commands.
- **No duplicate starters:** Never have both Docker Compose and direct process starts for the same service. Causes "address already in use" and violates single-owner principle.
- **Official deployment docs:** Follow Docker, Docker Compose, and FastAPI documentation for containerized deployment.

## Project rules

- **Production API:** Use Docker Compose as the single container orchestrator. All services run as containers with proper networking and health checks.
- **Scripts:** All deployment scripts delegate to Docker Compose commands (`docker compose up/down/restart`). Never start services directly outside containers.
- **Docs:** State clearly: production = Docker Compose orchestration; all services run in containers with proper isolation.

